  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nA whole-model 3D Pocket used the model's silhouette as its footprint, and the level law erodes that by the tool radius. So the cutter's edge never passed the silhouette. On a notch open to the part's outside, the pocket left a band one radius wide along the open edges at the full stock height, and the op reported `ok` (#1749).\r\n\r\n- `camcraft-motion`: new `machining3d::open_sides` (`machining3d/open_side.rs`). It grows the silhouette by the tool radius less 0.01 mm, minus a keep-out region. Where a level is open, the cutter centre now goes up to the silhouette edge. Where a level's material stands flush with the silhouette, the band is narrower than the erosion, so it cuts nothing there and a plain block gets no new ring.\r\n- `camcraft-app`: the new `operation/open_side.rs` applies this footprint in the Pocket3D arm and in the Multi-Axis Rough arm (the stamped twin: one ladder). It applies only to the source-built footprint of an untilted whole-model source. A picked or Boundary-controlled region, and a tilted plane, stay as before. The keep-out is the silhouette of the setup's other parts.\r\n- `keep_law::kept_models`: the setup's other parts now go into the solid law for Pocket3D and Multi-Axis Rough as a second net. This net also reports a cut through a second part that stands inside the model's own silhouette. Before, that cut read `ok` (the ladder's islands come only from its own model).\r\n- `shared_face_bodies`: the #1706 pin (`the_sample_as_imported_refuses_the_3d_pocket_by_name`) pinned the old law. No 6 mm tool fit inside the 6.53 mm strip, so the op refused. Under the new law the pocket clears the stock beside the strip with no gouge. The pin is renamed to `the_sample_as_imported_roughs_the_3d_pocket_beside_its_silhouette`. Recorded in `docs/decisions/1749-pocket3d-open-side.md`.\r\n  - The sample op does NOT post with the job's tool (takeover commit 82c9f082b). `EM-0600-4FL` has 15 mm of flute and an 8 mm shank; the part is 118 mm tall. Verify names `shank_hit` (part) and `rapid_in_stock` (the lifts out of those cuts), all `blocks_post`, and holds the post by R1. The test now deletes S1 (so the program gate runs) and asserts this reading by name: status `ok`, gate ran and passed, no gouge, only these two kinds, all on R1, `ok: false`, `held_by: [R1]`. Then it gives the tool 125 mm flutes and a 6 mm shank, generates again, and asserts a clean verify.\r\n  - Cause: the 3D Pocket ladder keeps only the flute radius off the material above a level. The same R1 moves with full-depth flutes give no findings. A closed cavity with no open side gives the same kinds with main's footprint law and with this PR's law. So the shank blindness is on main; this PR only gives the sample a path. It is owed in #1844 (P3).\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n\r\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_open_side.rs`. The fixture is built in code: a 30 mm block with its +X+Y quadrant notched down to Z 20, in a stock that fits it in XY with its top at Z 32. The tool is a 10 mm flat end mill, with offset rings and shell on.\r\n- `an_open_sided_notch_is_cleared_to_the_parts_edge`: measures the stock the path leaves (the lowest flat-end disc over each column) along both open edges, 0.05 mm inside the part edge. It must be at the floor, Z 20. It also checks that no feed disc enters the part's material at its Z, and that verify is clean. Before the fix, the stock stayed at Z 32.000 at (14.95, 10.80).\r\n- `an_open_side_never_reaches_into_a_neighbouring_part`: a second part 1 mm past the +X open edge. No feed disc comes within R of it, verify is clean, and the +Y open edge is still cleared.\r\n- `a_part_standing_in_the_notch_is_named_by_the_solid_law`: a second part on the notch floor, inside the model's silhouette, is reported (warnings > 0), not read as `ok`.\r\n\r\nMutation checks. Each mutation was reverted afterwards and the file compared byte-for-byte with its backup:\r\n- `open_footprint` returns the region unchanged: the open-edge test fails (stock at Z 32.000).\r\n- Keep-out made empty: the neighbour test fails (81 solid-law warnings; the second net fires).\r\n- The `keep_law` line removed: the neighbour test and the solid-law test both fail.\r\n\r\nGates (Linux):\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the Pocket3D-only version of the change: motion suites ok. App suites ok except `operations::multiaxis_rough_peels_the_same_ladder_and_poses_its_walls` (150 vs 134 moves). That failure led to the Multi-Axis Rough change. The #1706 pin also failed there; it is updated as described above.\r\n- After the final change, these targeted app suites, all green: operations, level_links, ribbon, suppressed_rest, rest_across_setups, stock_engine_agreement, setup_align, probe_op, remachining, drill_prior, area_controls, project_roundtrip, pocket3d_hsm, shared_face_bodies, keep_law, neighbour_law, kept_parts_live, coarse_laws, center_cut_multiaxis, pocket3d_open_side.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The takeover commit changes only the sample test and the decision file. Its quick gate (`--base 02892e348`) selects only that test.\r\n- `generate.rs` stays at 3668 lines (this PR adds 11). Its split is owed and is not done here.\r\n- Fixtures (vise jaws) are not subtracted from the open-side band. The decision file says so. The fixture laws of verify still judge them.\r\n- The tilted (3+2) case is owed in #1774 (PR #1780, stacked on this PR).\r\n\r\n- The full quick gate was not re-run on the final head; only the targeted suites listed above were. The motion crate did not change after the quick gate's green motion run.\r\n- No batch gate, heavy lanes, ui suites (`crates/ui/tests/operations.rs` uses Pocket3D) or snapshots.\r\n- A tilted (3+2) 3D Pocket keeps the old silhouette law, so it can still leave the ridge.\r\n- Stock that reaches more than about two radii past the silhouette is still not cleared by a whole-model 3D Pocket. That would be the stock-outline reading the 2D pocket has had since #12, which is a larger change. See the decision file.\r\n\r\nChangelog: A whole-model 3D Pocket (and Multi-Axis Rough) clears a notch open to the part's outside past its open edge instead of leaving a tool-radius ridge, keeps off the setup's other parts, and warns when it cuts through one.\r\n\r\nEffort: high (no escalation)\r\n\r\nFork synced at v0.19.0; branch made from upstream/main 4141eb1c.\r\n\r\nFixes #1749\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
